    "result_text": "All 70 tests pass with BUILD SUCCESS.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `riskFlag` field on the owner read model. It returns `true` when **any** of the three signals hold, otherwise `false`:\n\n1. **Possible duplicate** \u2014 reuses the stamped `possibleDuplicate` flag.\n2. **Disposable-adjacent email domain** \u2014 a new signal.\n3. **City over soft capacity** \u2014 reuses the stamped `capacityWarning` flag (the 40+ warning band below the hard cap of 50).\n\n### Changes\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only boolean `riskFlag` property to the `Owner` schema (so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it), documenting the three conditions.\n- **`DisposableDomains.java`** (new common helper) \u2014 made the disposable-domain blocklist the single source of truth, adding `domainOf`, `isBlocked`, and `isAdjacent`. *Disposable-adjacent* means a domain that is **not** itself blocked but is closely related to a blocked one \u2014 a subdomain of it, or one sharing a blocked provider's second-level label under a different TLD (e.g. `mailinator.net` next to blocked `mailinator.com`). Blocked domains themselves are rejected at create time, so they never reach this soft signal.\n- **`RejectDisposableEmailDomain.java`** \u2014 refactored to use `DisposableDomains` instead of its own inline blocklist (no behavior change to the reject rule).\n- **`RiskFlags.java`** (new common helper) \u2014 combines the three signals into `of(owner)`.\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a read-time mapping wiring `riskFlag` to `RiskFlags.of(owner)`, consistent with the other derived fields.\n\nThe `riskFlag` is derived at read time (like `contactPreference`, `ownerSegment`, etc.), drawing on the already-stamped `possibleDuplicate`/`capacityWarning` fields and the stored email, so `GET /api/owners/{id}` reflects it directly.\n\nOne design decision worth flagging: the task's \"disposable-adjacent\" term had no prior definition in the codebase, and the only test asserts the `false` case (an owner with no email). I chose a concrete, documented interpretation (subdomain-of / same-label-different-TLD). If you had a specific definition in mind for the *true* case, let me know and I'll adjust `DisposableDomains.isAdjacent`.",
